diff --git a/specs/state.md b/specs/state.md
index 26bd108..a96764a 100644
--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -577,6 +577,84 @@
   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Result Persistence Profile: `derived_pure_replay.v1`
+
+`result_persistence_profile` is an optional top-level `RunState` field (state
+schema stays `2.1`; the field is additive). Absent means the historical
+bundle-backed persistence: `to_dict()` omits the key and `from_dict()` of a
+payload without it yields `None`. The only supported present value is
+`derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other value fails closed with a `ValueError`
+naming the profile at `RunState` construction, at `StateManager.initialize`, and
+on load (a failed load never rewrites the state file). Ordinary loads never
+infer, backfill or upgrade the field; generic `initialize` callers opt in
+explicitly with `result_persistence_profile=`.
+
+**Selection.** The field is written atomically with the first state write, before
+any visit. A typed public `.orc` run (`orchestrator run`) and the new root of
+`orchestrator resume --force-restart` select the profile; the force-restart
+source run is left byte-for-byte unchanged and the new root keeps the requested
+observability settings. A fresh non-iterative child call frame selects it when
+the callee bundle's validated provenance has `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"`
+(never from the parent's profile, a path suffix, an alias or a step identity); a
+fresh retry after a failed non-iterative Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state
+and selects it. Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and
+iteration-owned child frames keep the historical profile, and an existing frame
+is never backfilled. A malformed existing frame (no `state`, or a non-mapping
+`state`) is rejected with a `ValueError` mentioning `existing call-frame state`
+before anything is written.
+
+**Eligibility.** A compiler-generated `pure_projection` is replay-eligible when it
+is acyclic and visited at most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned and other
+multiply visited pure nodes (`ineligible_pure_reasons[node_id]`, for example
+`multiple_visit_region`) keep full durable rows, bundles and checkpoints even
+inside a profiled root. Refs are scoped to the workflow that holds them; an
+imported callee bundle indexes only its own nodes. The index is derived by
+`orchestrator.workflow.pure_result_replay.derive_pure_result_replay_index` and
+never changes the serialized runtime plan.
+
+**Value-free completion shell.** Under the profile an eligible pure success is
+persisted as exactly:
+
+```json
+{"name": "<presentation_key>", "step_id": "<step_id>", "visit_count": 1,
+ "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+ "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution",
+             "class": "completed", "retryable": false},
+ "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}
+```
+
+Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. The full result stays in memory
+only. `StateManager.begin_eligible_pure_visit` (visit + running cursor),
+`reuse_interrupted_eligible_pure_visit`, `settle_eligible_pure_success` and
+`settle_eligible_pure_failure` are each one atomic state transaction.
+`classify_pure_replay_progress` classifies a node as `unstarted`, `interrupted`,
+`derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip` or `progress_witness_invalid` from its
+visit counter, cursor and row alone.
+
+**Resume.** Resume rebuilds only the pure values the remaining run reads, in
+memory, from validated durable inputs and rows, never dispatching an effect,
+incrementing a visit, settling a result or writing durable state. A resumed run
+fails closed before any effect with `error.type` `pure_result_replay_unavailable`
+and `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`,
+`durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`,
+`output_contract_invalid` (causes `materialize_ref_unresolved`,
+`pure_evaluation_failed`, `pure_projection_contract_invalid`) or
+`progress_witness_invalid` (rejected before the prologue). A persisted value row,
+pure result bundle, private lineage entry, checkpoint record or restore binding
+for an eligible node is a `profile_conflict` (`context.surface` is `steps`,
+`pure_bundle`, `private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record` or
+`restore_payload`), raised before the prologue or any state write.
+
+**Checkpoints.** Replay-eligible pure points emit no checkpoint record and are
+filtered out of the durable candidates before unique-nearest selection; their
+payloads omit derivable pure bindings. Default resume admits exactly one
+zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (mode
+`LEXICAL_CHECKPOINT_DEFAULT`, `checkpoint_id` null, `selection_reason`
+`validated_frame_entry_replay`), which requires validated bound-input leaves and
+exact profile and progress witnesses; without a durable owner it fails closed
+with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. Selection never
+scans past an invalid nearest durable boundary.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
